1
00:00:00,380 --> 00:00:04,556
Quick question. When you open a draft pack, how long does it take

2
00:00:04,556 --> 00:00:08,282
you to decide what you'd pick? That's the fun part for me.

3
00:00:10,932 --> 00:00:14,651
I love looking at a pack, weighing a couple of options, and

4
00:00:14,651 --> 00:00:18,180
finding out what another drafter would have done. It's a

5
00:00:18,180 --> 00:00:20,386
surprisingly fun thing to practice.

6
00:00:21,936 --> 00:00:25,904
That's why I built Pack One. It's a daily game around those

7
00:00:25,904 --> 00:00:30,276
individual decisions, without asking you to sit through an entire

8
00:00:30,276 --> 00:00:30,747
draft.

9
00:00:32,597 --> 00:00:36,891
Each challenge has eight picks from eight different real trophy

10
00:00:36,891 --> 00:00:40,912
drafts. Not eight picks from the same draft. Eight separate

11
00:00:40,912 --> 00:00:43,502
situations, each with its own context.

12
00:00:45,452 --> 00:00:49,364
You see the pack and what that player had already drafted. You

13
00:00:49,364 --> 00:00:53,340
make your choice, lock it in, and then find out what the trophy

14
00:00:53,340 --> 00:00:54,855
drafter actually picked.

15
00:00:56,905 --> 00:01:00,795
Sometimes you match their pick. Sometimes you still like your own

16
00:01:00,795 --> 00:01:04,626
choice better. Either way, there's something to think about, and

17
00:01:04,626 --> 00:01:07,260
maybe something to argue about with friends.

18
00:01:09,010 --> 00:01:12,850
At the end, you get a score and a Share button. Send it to your

19
00:01:12,850 --> 00:01:16,568
draft group and see who made the same calls. A different pick

20
00:01:16,568 --> 00:01:19,250
doesn't automatically mean it was a bad one.

21
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:25,601
There are three new Dailies every day. Draft Run, Powered Cube,

22
00:01:25,601 --> 00:01:29,093
and Latest Set. You can play one or try all three.

23
00:01:31,143 --> 00:01:35,280
If you like drafting, give Pack One a try. Pick your cards, share

24
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:39,480
your result, and tell me which decision you found the hardest. I'd

25
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:41,708
really like to hear what you think.
